    <description>WHAT IT DOES: Turns a form&apos;s Contact 2 answers (the second person on a form, or each family member captured in a repeater row) into a Person Account and hands it to the NPC Account engine. This is the mapping step: it decides which form fields land in which Account fields, and nothing else.

HOW IT WORKS, STEP BY STEP:
1. Setup loads the submission, template and section from the platform event.
2. Two small lookups prepare the record: the org&apos;s active person account Record Type, and the Person Account Contact 2 already points at (so a re-run updates rather than duplicates).
3. The Person Account (Field Map) transform is the heart of the flow and the reason to clone it: every line maps one form answer onto one Account field. The names, email, phone, birthdate and title always map; the mailing and other address blocks map only when the template&apos;s address sub-rules are on, so curated addresses are not overwritten by blank form answers. IsPersonAccount, the record type and the existing Id and PersonContactId ride along so the engine knows exactly what it is saving.
4. The record goes to the single NPC Account engine, together with the template&apos;s Contact matching rules, and the engine does the rest: strip, match, save, log, follow-ups.

WHERE IT FITS: Installed by the Alternate Contact record of Form Template Conversion Mapping Default. To change WHICH FIELDS a person gets from a form, clone this flow, adjust the transform, and point the template&apos;s override hook (or the custom metadata) at your clone; matching and saving behaviour lives in the engine, not here. NOTE ON COUNTRY AND STATE PICKLISTS: rendering Country and State as picklists on a form requires the Custom Address fields feature to be enabled and configured on the Form Submission object; the answers then arrive on the custom Address field&apos;s components instead of the plain text fields this map reads, so update the address lines of this field map accordingly.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>True when the Contact 2 Set Mailing Address rule is enabled; address mapping stays opt-in so matches never silently overwrite curated addresses.</description>
        <name>AssignMailingAddress</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>IF({!PlatformEvent.Type__c} == {!Contact1_FieldApiName},
IF({!FormSubmission.Internal_Is_Related_Record__c},
ISPICKVAL({!PageSection.Conversion_Rule__c},&apos;Contact1 👉 Set Mailing Address&apos;),
INCLUDES({!FormSubmission.Form_Template__r.Conversion_Rules__c},&apos;Contact1 👉 Set Mailing Address&apos;)
),
IF({!PlatformEvent.Type__c} == {!Contact2_FieldApiName},
if({!FormSubmission.Internal_Is_Related_Record__c},
ISPICKVAL({!PageSection.Conversion_Rule__c},&apos;Contact2 👉 Set Mailing Address&apos;),
INCLUDES({!FormSubmission.Form_Template__r.Conversion_Rules__c},&apos;Contact2 👉 Set Mailing Address&apos;)
),
false))</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>True when the Contact 2 Set Other Address rule is enabled.</description>
        <name>AssignOtherAddress</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>IF({!PlatformEvent.Type__c} == {!Contact1_FieldApiName},
IF({!FormSubmission.Internal_Is_Related_Record__c},
ISPICKVAL({!PageSection.Conversion_Rule__c},&apos;Contact1 👉 Set Other Address&apos;),
INCLUDES({!FormSubmission.Form_Template__r.Conversion_Rules__c},&apos;Contact1 👉 Set Other Address&apos;)
),
IF({!PlatformEvent.Type__c} == {!Contact2_FieldApiName},
if({!FormSubmission.Internal_Is_Related_Record__c},
ISPICKVAL({!PageSection.Conversion_Rule__c},&apos;Contact2 👉 Set Other Address&apos;),
INCLUDES({!FormSubmission.Form_Template__r.Conversion_Rules__c},&apos;Contact2 👉 Set Other Address&apos;)
),
false))</expression>
    </formulas>
